{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Answered the last open point from source: send_accsync picks the follower's valid entries index as its reported accepted index (3) when the promise matches the leader's ballot, at most 3 when it matches the earlier round, and the follower's decided index (4) otherwise, and create_log_sync starts the suffix there while sync_log rewrites only from sync_idx onward. Every branch therefore leaves the missing index 2 below the sync boundary, so recovery cannot refill it. Recorded that as behavior, attached it to the restart question, and restated the account with the measured reload plus the recovery bound. Validation is valid with execution_requested false. The bound is source-derived, assumes the non-snapshot sync path, and the recovery messages themselves were never delivered.\"}"}}
